        <p>BROUGHTON 2ND V. WARRINGTON 2ND.—At Broughton, on Saturday. Warrington batted first and opened the innings with Bibby and Dutton. Runs came freely, Dutton hitting out until howled off his lees for 14. Bibby continued to bat carefully, and scored 24, when a good ball took the bails. iNith the score at 59,Isherwood and Hampson got together, and these two batsmen offered a determined resistance to the bowling, arid carried the score to 104, before Ilampson was sent back for a well played 23. The innings closed for 118, Isher- wood being not out 30. When stumps were drawn the home side had scored 148 for eight wickets, Piercy be- ing top scorer with 31. Brown was the most successful bowler for the visitors, taking four wickets for 20 runs. Score :</p>
