        <p>FARLESTOWN V. LLANDTIDNO.—EarIPstown paid a visit to Llandudno, on Saturday, to fulfil an engage- ment with the seaside club, when a triGst successful day was spent. The party numbering 30, left Earlestown at 9 o'clock, arriving at their destination at 12-15. The match was advertised for 2 o'clock. and punctuagy, at that hour play commenced . The visitors won the toss, Sanders and Barker batting first. The ground was in excellent run-getting order, and both men made good uso of their opportunities. carrying the score to 68, at which total Barker was bowled, after 'contributing 33, being shortly afterwards followed by Sanders, who had also made 33. Noires for once in a way did not trouble the scorers very much, and Miller knocked up 23, in a few minutes. Husband who partnered him played a good innings of 17, but it was left to Bates to make ! the score of the day ; going in the sixth he took out his bat for a good innings of 35. Of the remainder Clare I was a long way the best, being bowled by Osborne for 17. The whole side batted well, ar.d though the bowling could not be styled first-class, and the fielding could have been at times improed upon, yet, on the wnole, 185 vrasa fair total. 'flue home team bear a very fair name for their batting powers, and as they have lately been knocking up some very tall scores, they considered they had a tnoderate chance of winning, but a very few overs upset their calculations, as tour of the best on the side had left with only 11 runs on Bibby, Vincent-Walker and Foulds then put on better appearance on the game, but after they were disposed of, the rest were only a 1. moderate lot, the side being all one for 66. 'f he Welsh- ' men were a little surprised at the result, such beatings • being of rare occurrence with thetn.as out of the matches played so far, only one had ended in a defeat 6 runs. Score:—</p>
        <p>EARLESTOWN. I.LaNnunNts J Sanders b Bibby T Barker b Roberts 33 J. J Marks b Cable J Miller c Bibby b GF A Osborne b Hopkins 0 Roberts W 11 Noises c Bibby b Clarke b Hopkins Roberts G Husband c A b Roberts 17 b Hopkins ll R Bates not out 35 F Foulds b Bates ll J 11 Alderson c Walker b Webb h Hopkins 4 Clarke 7 H W Jones c Clare b Hop - F P Clare b 04borne ....« 17 kills 0 G H Hopillis b Osborne 4 W Wood St Husband b A J Cable c and b Osborne 7 Bates C W Emmett c Wood b H E Roberts not out Clarke Extras 3 Extras 4</p>
