        <p>COUNTY SCORING.</p>
        <p>The following are the returns up to date of the teams in the championship and association competitions : Hindsford, 239-201 ; Warrington, 235-185 ; cr,-,res Bank, 231-211-208 ; Stretford, 229 : Leigh, 227-218; Chorlton, 221-199 ; Isle of Man, 220-197 ; Broughton, 212-204; Wigan, 209 ; Cheethain Hill, 200 ; Barlow Moor, 192 ; Didsbury, 189 ; Broalands, 183-174 ; Urinston, 181. THE AMATEUR CHAMPIONSHIP. The sub-committee of the County Association have Axed upon 'Blackpool for the annual Individual Merit Cmnpetitions, and having visited toe several greens at that popular seaside resort, have decided upon the one attached to the Queen's Hotel, in Talbot-road, as best suitable for the purpose. In accordance with the expressed wish of the majority of the players in the Lancashire team, the return contest Yorkshire v. Lan- cashire wilt take place over the Midland green at With- ington. QUOITS.</p>
        <p>WAHRENGTON V. CLAIIMITON.—A match was played on Saturday between the above clubs on the Claughton ground, the home team winning by 40 shots.</p>
