      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1893-07-08_WidnesExaminer_art0082" n="art0082">
        <head>ALLEGED THEFII-011 A WATCH AT</head>
        <p>ALLEGED THEFII-011 A WATCH AT</p>
        <p>--- HAYDOCK. - At the Warr ington Occasional Court on Thurs- day beton&gt; Mi .W.Mortimer,Ann Griin.iihaw,a tramp, was charged with stealing a silver watch and metal guard from a dwelling-house at'llaydock, on Wed- nesday aft, moon, the property ot Mr. Oliver Ped- lar. It appe era from the evidence of the complain- ant that ab mt three o'clock on Wednesday afterncmn, he went to wash himself in the back scullery, and placed his watch on the window ledge. After washing himself he went u pstairs leaving his watch behind him. While upstairs ?lie heard a knock at the door but he never answerty lit, and soon afterwards he heard the door onen as d then close again. Ho looked fr. m the windog • and saw the prisoner going away from the house.: On coming downstairs ho missed Ids watch, and immef',iately followed ber,snd informed the police. She was P pprehended by P.C. Williams, and the watch was font/ din her possession. The prisoner was remanded une,l Saturday hi order that further inquiries might.be ma- de.</p>
